  "notes": "Hard, minimal 808-and-bell. Two parameters carry it. The first is harmonic-minor colour in the leads — `scales` puts `harmonic_minor` level with `natural_minor` at weight 4 each, which no other single-riff entry on this bench does, and the raised seventh is what makes the bell figure sound like his rather than like the generic dark-trap motif. The second is that the 808 is described as the record's mass: `distortion` heavy with `distortionWet` [0.25,0.55], `slideProb` 0.6, and `bassline.glideProb` 0.6, sitting under a melody of only 2–5 notes a bar. The claps are hard and layered, so `layerClapOffsetMs` is the tightest pair in this batch at [1,4] — a stacked clap that reads as one hit rather than a room. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it medium and marks the harmonic detail [LOW-CONF]: the DAW and credits are confirmed but the harmony is partly inferred, so `chords` and the `harmonic_minor` weighting are the inferred parameters here, not the drums. ⚠ `chords.impliedByRiff` is set because the research says single-riff productions over a static tonic. The i–VI family at weight 2 is INFERRED and exists so the generated chord part reaches its distinct-output floor; the research names no motion at all.",
